.SH NAME
maknoon-serve - Start the Maknoon PQC API Server (MCP/SSE)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmaknoon serve [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Launches the Maknoon API server. All cryptographic and vault operations
are exposed via the MCP SSE transport. Kubernetes liveness and readiness probes
are available at /v1/live and /v1/ready respectively.

.PP
The server mandates Post-Quantum TLS 1.3 (ML-KEM hybrid) for all connections,
ensuring a zero-trust, quantum-resistant infrastructure.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--address\fP=":8081"
	Address to listen on

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for serve

.PP
\fB--tls-cert\fP=""
	Path to TLS certificate (REQUIRED)

.PP
\fB--tls-key\fP=""
	Path to TLS private key (REQUIRED)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--fips\fP[=false]
	Enforce strict FIPS-140 compliant cryptographic standards

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output results in JSON format

.PP
\fB--policy\fP=""
	Path to a declarative governance policy file (JSON)

.PP
\fB--tpm\fP[=false]
	Enable TPM 2.0 hardware-backed storage for keys

.PP
\fB--tpm-device\fP="/dev/tpmrm0"
	Path to the TPM device node

.PP
\fB--tpm-pcrs\fP=[]
	List of PCRs to bind keys to (e.g., 7,14)

.PP
\fB--trace\fP[=false]
	Enable low-level diagnostic tracing to stderr


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmaknoon(1)\fP


